# up-to-actual — Cron Configuration
#
# Install with: crontab -e (then paste the relevant line)
#
# Logs are appended to a file and rotated via logrotate or size.
# Adjust paths to match your installation directory.

# ── Sync (daily at 2am Melbourne time) ───────────────────────
# The system cron uses the host timezone. Ensure your Raspberry Pi
# is set to Australia/Melbourne:
#   sudo timedatectl set-timezone Australia/Melbourne
#
0 2 * * * cd /opt/up-to-actual && /usr/bin/node src/index.js >> /var/log/up-to-actual/sync.log 2>&1

# ── Health check (every 6 hours, for Uptime Kuma push monitor) ─
# Optional: validates connectivity to Up Bank and Actual Budget.
# Configure Uptime Kuma with a "Push" monitor and append the push
# URL to the command, e.g.:
#   && curl -fsS -o /dev/null https://kuma.local/api/push/xxxxx
#
0 */6 * * * cd /opt/up-to-actual && /usr/bin/node src/healthcheck.js >> /var/log/up-to-actual/healthcheck.log 2>&1

# ── Log rotation ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create /etc/logrotate.d/up-to-actual with:
#
#   /var/log/up-to-actual/*.log {
#       weekly
#       rotate 4
#       compress
#       missingok
#       notifempty
#   }
